# Normalize every text file to LF, on checkout and in the repository, regardless of the checking-out
# machine's own core.autocrlf. Found necessary by a real, reproducible failure: GitHub Actions'
# windows-latest runners default Git for Windows to core.autocrlf=true, so a multi-line C# raw string
# literal (NotesYamlRoundTripTests' own Markdown constant, among others) is compiled with \r\n on that
# runner and \n everywhere else — the literal itself differs by platform before a single line of test
# code ever runs, which is a strictly worse problem than any individual test working around it. `auto`
# lets git's own binary-detection heuristic exempt genuinely binary files; explicit entries below are
# only for the handful of extensions where guessing wrong would actually matter.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched by line-ending normalization — corrupts binary content if it is.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.zip binary
*.nupkg binary
